1
00:01:41,759 --> 00:01:44,400
For a moment, I really hoped all this

2
00:01:45,080 --> 00:01:46,600
was just a dream.

3
00:01:47,720 --> 00:01:51,000
That we could start over and continue when we woke up.

4
00:01:52,240 --> 00:01:53,370
I'll help you today.

5
00:01:54,039 --> 00:01:55,360
You must succeed.

6
00:02:12,360 --> 00:02:12,560
Su.

7
00:02:16,960 --> 00:02:18,560
So Xiaofei still died.

8
00:02:20,320 --> 00:02:22,650
From the moment it wanted to eat that cake,

9
00:02:23,240 --> 00:02:25,079
the ending was already predetermined.

10
00:02:25,079 --> 00:02:26,000
It's okay.

11
00:02:26,840 --> 00:02:29,040
We've already changed part of history.

12
00:02:29,960 --> 00:02:31,290
I threw the helmet away,

13
00:02:31,880 --> 00:02:34,200
so Mara can't hide under it.

14
00:02:35,040 --> 00:02:36,720
Now we just need to protect Xiaotao

15
00:02:36,720 --> 00:02:38,650
and try to change the final ending.

16
00:02:40,360 --> 00:02:41,240
And then?

17
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:45,730
What happens after we succeed?

18
00:02:48,320 --> 00:02:50,380
If you had achieved success earlier,

19
00:02:51,520 --> 00:02:53,200
would we not have broken up?

20
00:02:53,920 --> 00:02:55,560
Would the pain be lessened?

21
00:02:56,160 --> 00:02:57,820
Could everything start over?

22
00:02:59,600 --> 00:03:01,400
What matters now is not the past,

23
00:03:01,840 --> 00:03:03,770
but life and death, and the future.

24
00:03:05,800 --> 00:03:07,720
If we all die here today,

25
00:03:07,960 --> 00:03:08,960
how can there be a tomorrow?

26
00:03:08,960 --> 00:03:10,360
How can there be a future?

27
00:03:17,560 --> 00:03:19,920
I remember at this time before the banquet,

28
00:03:19,920 --> 00:03:21,980
we should be resting in our own rooms.

29
00:03:25,480 --> 00:03:26,680
Old Dai is here.

30
00:03:28,960 --> 00:03:30,560
Why did he come down so early?

31
00:03:30,840 --> 00:03:32,160
Are you scared now?

32
00:03:32,920 --> 00:03:33,920
To help you,

33
00:03:34,160 --> 00:03:35,600
I'd risk everything.

34
00:03:35,680 --> 00:03:38,160
Don't think you can brush me off with your lousy money.

35
00:03:38,160 --> 00:03:39,320
I'm warning you.

36
00:03:39,440 --> 00:03:40,680
If you dare betray me

37
00:03:41,120 --> 00:03:42,960
and get back together with An'an,

38
00:03:42,960 --> 00:03:45,360
even your life won't be enough to pay for it.

39
00:03:49,160 --> 00:03:50,640
I'm in control now.

40
00:03:52,920 --> 00:03:54,250
If you don't want to die,

41
00:03:55,240 --> 00:03:56,300
don't mess with me.

42
00:04:08,320 --> 00:04:09,040
Mr. Dai.

43
00:04:10,320 --> 00:04:11,680
Beautiful Su,

44
00:04:12,080 --> 00:04:13,120
what are your orders?

45
00:04:13,120 --> 00:04:16,079
The bottle you said tasted as good as Romanée-Conti...

46
00:04:16,079 --> 00:04:17,339
which one was it again?

47
00:04:17,880 --> 00:04:19,120
The black one in the wine cabinet.

48
00:04:19,120 --> 00:04:20,079
Let's go. I'll take you to get it.

49
00:04:20,079 --> 00:04:21,940
That's going to cost you, Mr. Dai.

50
00:04:22,480 --> 00:04:24,010
What are you talking about?

51
00:04:24,280 --> 00:04:25,740
It's just a bottle of wine.

52
00:04:26,480 --> 00:04:28,760
Besides, Beautiful Su is a wine connoisseur.

53
00:04:28,760 --> 00:04:29,440
If you want a drink,

54
00:04:29,440 --> 00:04:30,160
anytime.

55
00:04:30,520 --> 00:04:31,720
But such a fine wine,

56
00:04:33,720 --> 00:04:36,320
I only want to drink it alone with Beautiful Su.

57
00:04:38,200 --> 00:04:40,400
I don't just drink with anyone.

58
00:04:40,440 --> 00:04:42,300
Once your contract is finalized,

59
00:04:42,560 --> 00:04:43,880
we can celebrate.

60
00:04:46,880 --> 00:04:49,340
You're here to speak for Zhiwei, aren't you?

61
00:04:51,320 --> 00:04:52,720
I'm a simple person.

62
00:04:52,880 --> 00:04:54,200
When Zhiwei is happy,

63
00:04:54,320 --> 00:04:55,280
I'm happy.

64
00:04:55,720 --> 00:04:57,520
But don't tell him that.

65
00:04:57,520 --> 00:04:59,250
I'm afraid he'll get too proud.

66
00:04:59,320 --> 00:05:01,720
I used to think love wasn't that important.

67
00:05:02,560 --> 00:05:04,520
Only at this moment did I realize

68
00:05:05,760 --> 00:05:07,280
I pretended not to need it,

69
00:05:07,960 --> 00:05:09,840
not because it's insignificant,

70
00:05:10,440 --> 00:05:12,600
but because the cost is too high.

71
00:05:14,520 --> 00:05:16,520
Isn't it just a copyright contract?

72
00:05:16,880 --> 00:05:18,520
Since you asked,

73
00:05:19,200 --> 00:05:20,720
I definitely have to

74
00:05:21,480 --> 00:05:23,000
do you this favor.

75
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:38,130
Don't be impulsive.

76
00:05:38,320 --> 00:05:41,050
I understand my task is to save tonight's ending.

77
00:05:41,760 --> 00:05:43,520
But in this situation,

78
00:05:43,960 --> 00:05:45,760
I believe no man

79
00:05:45,760 --> 00:05:47,600
could stay calm.

80
00:06:07,680 --> 00:06:08,520
So,

81
00:06:08,760 --> 00:06:11,400
do you really believe I was also involved in 'The Death of Marat'?

82
00:06:11,400 --> 00:06:12,400
I believe it.

83
00:06:12,400 --> 00:06:14,040
Such a complex perspective

84
00:06:14,240 --> 00:06:16,570
must not be just one person's experience.

85
00:06:17,000 --> 00:06:18,840
It's like a record

86
00:06:18,840 --> 00:06:20,440
and witness of a conspiracy.

87
00:06:21,800 --> 00:06:23,120
I also believe

88
00:06:23,120 --> 00:06:25,520
the time travel in the book is real.

89
00:06:27,240 --> 00:06:28,160
If a person

90
00:06:28,360 --> 00:06:29,920
can control time,

91
00:06:30,920 --> 00:06:32,840
is there anything they can't do?

92
00:06:34,240 --> 00:06:35,760
And what failure

93
00:06:36,040 --> 00:06:37,640
is unavoidable?

94
00:06:40,120 --> 00:06:42,760
Even if you kill someone this way,

95
00:06:43,320 --> 00:06:44,960
an alibi

96
00:06:46,200 --> 00:06:47,680
can be easily created.

97
00:06:48,680 --> 00:06:50,280
Sometimes,

98
00:06:51,159 --> 00:06:52,480
doing the right thing

99
00:06:53,280 --> 00:06:55,080
is as hard as committing a crime.

100
00:06:57,760 --> 00:07:00,890
This is the ingenuity you writers want to convey, right?

101
00:07:01,960 --> 00:07:02,840
An'an.

102
00:07:03,960 --> 00:07:05,680
Why do I feel like

103
00:07:06,160 --> 00:07:07,640
you're different since you came back?

104
00:07:07,640 --> 00:07:08,600
Yeah.

105
00:07:09,920 --> 00:07:12,720
People can't be trapped in the same place forever,

106
00:07:12,720 --> 00:07:13,880
unable to change.

107
00:07:38,880 --> 00:07:40,610
What are you doing with a knife?

108
00:07:42,400 --> 00:07:43,960
Who are you going to dissect now?

109
00:07:43,960 --> 00:07:46,020
I don't need you to ask Mr. Dai for help

110
00:07:46,720 --> 00:07:48,580
and do things you don't want to do.

111
00:07:51,200 --> 00:07:53,400
You heard my conversation with Mr. Dai.

112
00:07:55,120 --> 00:07:55,840
Because you were bullied

113
00:07:55,840 --> 00:07:57,100
and never fought back,

114
00:07:58,720 --> 00:08:02,050
you've kept it hidden in your heart for so many years, right?

115
00:08:03,560 --> 00:08:05,680
Because the world owes you an apology,

116
00:08:05,680 --> 00:08:06,560
you can't let it go.

117
00:08:06,560 --> 00:08:07,400
Am I right?

118
00:08:20,800 --> 00:08:22,440
I'm sorry, Sophie.

119
00:08:24,520 --> 00:08:27,050
I don't need you to use the way you hate the most

120
00:08:27,760 --> 00:08:29,760
to endure the unbearable pain

121
00:08:31,680 --> 00:08:32,940
you least want to face.

122
00:08:36,000 --> 00:08:37,520
You got angry for me.

123
00:08:38,840 --> 00:08:40,500
There is someone in this world

124
00:08:40,760 --> 00:08:42,240
who cares about me

125
00:08:43,559 --> 00:08:45,420
and is willing to get angry for me.

126
00:08:48,480 --> 00:08:49,880
So it's fine now.

127
00:08:52,200 --> 00:08:52,920
It's like

128
00:08:53,800 --> 00:08:55,160
there's an old,

129
00:08:55,400 --> 00:08:56,480
un-washable stain

130
00:08:56,600 --> 00:08:57,880
in my heart.

131
00:09:00,800 --> 00:09:02,320
It can be very clean

132
00:09:03,080 --> 00:09:04,000
and new.

133
00:09:06,600 --> 00:09:07,760
I really like it.

134
00:09:31,160 --> 00:09:31,800
It's fine.

135
00:09:32,360 --> 00:09:33,480
I'll do it myself.

136
00:09:33,480 --> 00:09:33,800
Take a rest.

137
00:09:33,800 --> 00:09:35,160
I'll go and do it myself.

138
00:09:38,760 --> 00:09:39,760
Why are you here?

139
00:09:40,160 --> 00:09:42,040
Weren't you going to stake out the man in black?

140
00:09:42,040 --> 00:09:43,700
I'm not that brother of yours.

141
00:09:43,720 --> 00:09:44,080
No.

142
00:09:44,480 --> 00:09:47,200
Which one of you is the older brother?

143
00:09:48,480 --> 00:09:49,720
I came back from 12 o'clock.

144
00:09:49,720 --> 00:09:51,320
He came back from 10 o'clock.

145
00:09:51,320 --> 00:09:52,360
The current me

146
00:09:52,720 --> 00:09:53,840
is here to save you.

147
00:09:53,840 --> 00:09:55,100
What nonsense is this?

148
00:09:55,520 --> 00:09:56,120
Man.

149
00:09:57,840 --> 00:10:00,360
Are you crazy?

150
00:10:00,760 --> 00:10:02,280
Stay away from Su Fei.

151
00:10:04,440 --> 00:10:05,700
What's wrong with you?

152
00:10:07,680 --> 00:10:08,940
Keep an eye on him here.

153
00:10:11,840 --> 00:10:12,520
Don't worry, Xiaotao.

154
00:10:12,520 --> 00:10:13,520
We've been brothers for ten years.

155
00:10:13,520 --> 00:10:15,240
No matter what, I won't hurt you.

156
00:10:15,240 --> 00:10:16,480
Today is a good day.

157
00:10:17,560 --> 00:10:19,800
We must sign this contract.

158
00:10:25,440 --> 00:10:27,040
Why is only your name on this?

159
00:10:27,520 --> 00:10:28,800
Isn't that obvious?

160
00:10:28,800 --> 00:10:30,560
He wrote the novel alone.

161
00:10:30,560 --> 00:10:32,760
Of course you can only write his name.

162
00:10:33,480 --> 00:10:34,160
Xiaotao.

163
00:10:34,560 --> 00:10:37,160
We can't have the same argument all over again.

164
00:10:38,280 --> 00:10:38,760
Look.

165
00:10:39,520 --> 00:10:40,320
Trust me.

166
00:10:40,320 --> 00:10:41,320
I will handle it well.

167
00:10:41,320 --> 00:10:43,160
I absolutely won't let you see this happen again.

168
00:10:43,160 --> 00:10:45,480
How long are you going to keep this from me?

169
00:10:45,480 --> 00:10:45,960
Great.

170
00:10:47,120 --> 00:10:49,520
Brothers turning against each other.

171
00:10:49,920 --> 00:10:53,040
This detail must be written into the novel.

172
00:10:53,760 --> 00:10:54,560
Great.
